  "description": "Versioned fixture corpus for the deterministic ECZ result-slip parser. Each case is the OCR TEXT layer a server Tesseract read produces for one representative slip (the parser's real input). `slip_truth` is what a human reads from the slip; `expected` pins the parser's required behaviour. Accuracy is measured against `slip_truth`, so a case the parser deliberately withholds (low confidence, duplicate) counts as recall loss rather than being quietly redefined as success.",
  "capture": {
    "mode": "recorded_text",
    "notes": "Text layers are authored/recorded to match the line shapes real Tesseract output produces for Zambian ECZ statements of results: dot leaders, row numbering, bracketed letter descriptors, and character damage. Add `image` to a case to have the evaluator run live Tesseract (pytesseract + a tesseract binary) end to end; without an image, or without Tesseract installed, the recorded text layer is used and the report states which mode ran."
  },
  "thresholds": {
    "min_precision": 1.0,
    "min_recall": 0.85,
    "min_mean_confidence": 0.8,
    "max_wrong_confirmable": 0
  },
